{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And you shall speak to all who are wise of heart.</b> He mentioned here as well two direct addresses — 'and you shall speak' — because all who are wise of heart received the emanation from Moses, as it is written (Numbers 11:17), ״וְאָצַלְתִּי מִן הָרוּחַ אֲשֶׁר עָלֶיךָ וְשַׂמְתִּי עֲלֵיהֶם״. And likewise all the makers of the craft who were in the shade of El received the influx of wisdom through the mediation of Moses, as it is written (Exodus 18:21), ״וְאַתָּה תֶחֱזֶה מִכָּל הָעָם״ — that is, through the holy spirit that is upon you. And it means that you shall cause to flow upon the judges of Israel from the holy spirit that is upon you. So too, ״וְאַתָּה תְּדַבֵּר אֶל כָּל חַכְמֵי לֵב״ — in order that they may receive the emanation of the light of insight from you. Therefore it is said at the completion of all the work of the Tabernacle, ״וַיְכַל מֹשֶׁה אֶת הַמְּלָאכָה״ (Exodus 40:33) — but did Moses complete the work? Was it not all who were wise of heart who made it! Rather, because Moses emanated upon them from the light of his insight, it is as though he himself made all the work. And He said, ״אֲשֶׁר מִלֵּאתִיו רוּחַ חָכְמָה״ — that is to say: even though in truth I filled him with the spirit of wisdom, for ״ה׳ יִתֵּן חָכְמָה״ (Proverbs 2:6), nevertheless since the influx reaches them through your mediation, everything is called by your name. Therefore it says ״וְאַתָּה״ — from the essence of your very being and the additional wisdom that is in you — ״תְּדַבֵּר אֶל כָּל חַכְמֵי לֵב״ to cause it to flow upon them. And since it says ״חַכְמֵי לֵב״ in the plural, it should have said ״אֲשֶׁר מִלֵּאתִים רוּחַ חָכְמָה״. We can say that ״מִלֵּאתִיו״ refers back to Moses — for because I filled him with the spirit of wisdom, therefore he will emanate from his wisdom upon all who are wise of heart. And this is not a statement of HaShem, blessed be He, to Moses — for if so He should have said ״אֲשֶׁר מִלֵּאתִיךָ רוּחַ חָכְמָה״ — rather, the verse explains to us the meaning of what I said to Moses, ״וְאַתָּה תְּדַבֵּר אֶל כָּל חַכְמֵי לֵב״ — why do I suspend the matter upon Moses? Because I filled him with the spirit of wisdom. And afterward the Holy One, blessed be He, turned back and said to Moses directly, ״וְעָשׂוּ אֶת בִּגְדֵי אַהֲרֹן״, etc. And the word ״אֲשֶׁר״ functions as 'because,' as is its usage in several places."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:23:53.080902535Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}